From ecedb74cf6571feb937ccf447dbd94152b308b1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 18:05:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(vercel): the merged config that actually shipped, and
 CORS on every machine surface
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patch 78 did not land. The delete of the superseded 77 ran, then ship.sh step 1
did git reset --hard origin/main and restored it, because 77 was tracked on main
from the upload. ship.sh applied the only patch it could see, so commit 50fc9fc
carries 77's contents under 78's message: every guard green, deploy verdict ✓,
and the merged vercel.json, the twenty-seventh guard and the deletion of
old-domain/vercel.json all silently absent. This is the delta.

One vercel.json for both domains. Three host-scoped edge redirects — both forms
of the old domain plus www.ecowoods.ca → apex, which was never handled anywhere
and is a second unconsolidated host on the canonical domain itself. Evaluated at
the edge before the request reaches Next: one hop, no function invocation. The
next.config.js rules stay as a fallback and cannot chain.

old-domain/vercel.json deleted. Its rule has no host condition — correct in a
project serving only the old domain, catastrophic pasted here, where it matches
every request on ecowoods.ca and redirects the site to itself. A 301 loop is
cached by browsers and CDNs, so it outlives the rollback.

The biggest single fix is CORS. /llms.txt, /llms-full.txt, /ai.txt,
/api/knowledge and every .md now send Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *. Those
surfaces exist to be fetched by agents and without the header a browser-context
fetch is blocked — seven machine editions were being published to clients that
could not read them, in a config file nobody thought to audit.

Also X-Frame-Options DENY → SAMEORIGIN, which was blocking the site from framing
its own pages and contradicting frame-ancestors 'self' in the CSP;
X-XSS-Protection 1; mode=block → 0, deprecated and itself an XSS vector;
immutable caching on /_next/static and /brand; text/markdown on .md; and
X-Robots-Tag max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large.

verify-vercel-config.mjs is the twenty-seventh guard and it fails on all six
failure modes, proven by injection including the exact paste.

Old domain host identified: Apache/2.4.68 (Debian). old-domain/.htaccess is the
file; EXECUTE.md and the README now say so at the top instead of asking.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
